       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as you confirmed it: **metformin 1700 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals**. The order ID is **ORD-0001**.\n\nI added a note saying the total is 5100 mg/day, which is above the labeled maximum, and that you confirmed the dose after it was flagged. The note also says no clinical reason has been recorded yet and asks for pharmacist review.\n\n**Before the first dose:**\n- **Pharmacy will likely contact you.** Adding a short reason to the chart now could make that faster.\n- **If this dose is intended**, watch for GI side effects (nausea, vomiting, diarrhea) and signs of lactic acidosis, especially if kidney function changes or the patient gets contrast dye, becomes septic or hypoxic, or gets dehydrated.\n- **If 1700 mg was meant as the daily total**, let me know and I'll change it to 850 mg twice daily."
